  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Wheel and rack",
  "exampleId": "block-wheel-road",
  "description": "A constant 30 N·m on a 0.3 m wheel pushes the 100 kg vehicle with 100 N against 10 N·s/m of drag, so it approaches 10 m/s with a time constant of about 10 s (the wheel inertia adds 1.1 kg). The rack and pinion turns 100 rad per metre, so a pinion at 10 rad/s moves the rack 0.1 m every second.",
